     "merged_at": "2026-06-29T11:03:44Z"
    },
    "body": "## Summary\n\nIntroduce a per-shard rayon thread pool for edge shards and use it to parallelize both segment loading and per-segment read operations.\n\n- Add `EdgeConfig::max_search_threads` (`Option<usize>`; `None` or `0` resolves to the CPU-derived default via `common::defaults::search_thread_count`, matching the core search runtime). Exposed through the builder and Python bindings.\n- Build a long-lived search pool in `EdgeShard` and `ReadOnlyEdgeShard` (`pool::build_search_pool`); pool creation failures return `OperationError` instead of panicking during shard open.\n- Add `EdgeReadView::par_map_segments` as the single seam for parallel per-segment work; wire it into search, scroll, count, facet, and rescore-with-formula.\n- Add `load_segments_parallel` and use it in `ReadOnlyEdgeShard::open_with_enumerator` and `refresh` to open segments in parallel outside the holder write lock, reducing follower startup and refresh latency for shards with many segments.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `cargo test -p edge read_only` \u2014 all tests pass\n- [x] CI green (lint, rust-tests, integration-tests, Test Qdrant Edge, e2e-tests)\n\nMade with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)",
